{
    "_meta": {
        "title": "Lipsync / Talking Photo (InfiniteTalk)",
        "description": "Core ComfyUI nodes only. Wan 2.1 I2V 480p fp8 + lightx2v cfg/step-distill LoRA (6 steps, euler/normal, CFG 1) patched with the InfiniteTalk single-speaker model patch; wav2vec2 encodes the speech, which drives the mouth/head. The photo is the start image + CLIP-vision reference. One WanInfiniteTalkToVideo pass = 81 frames @ 25 fps; the builder (src/lib/oj/lipsync.ts) chains extra passes (previous_frames, 9 motion frames, +72 new frames each) until the audio is covered (capped), trims frames to the audio length and trims the audio to match, then CreateVideo muxes the speech into the mp4."
    },
